    "https://uottawa.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uOttawa_External_Career_Site/job/Main-Campus/ATPUO---Winter-2027---ADM4311M---Strategic-Management_JR38772": {
      "title": "ATPUO - Winter 2027 - ADM4311M - Strategic Management",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosting Reason: New Position Location: Ottawa, ON Academic Period: 2027 Winter Semester Faculty: École de gestion Telfer / Telfer School of Management Academic Unit: Telfer School of Management Course Title: Strategic Management Course Code: ADM4311 Section: M Course Description: This course integrates knowledge attained from prior courses combined with the latest strategy frameworks and analytical concepts. Students must examine and resolve the complex decisions top managers face in today's globally competitive world. Pedagogically, the course utilizes the case study method, which encourages student centered learning, real business analysis, and group participation. As an introductory course in strategy, the emphasis is placed on the fundamental tools of strategic formulation, competitive and market analysis, developing resource and organizational capabilities, shaping strategic fit, and leading organizational integration, with the aim of improving a firm's long-term performance. Posting limited to: Professeur à temps-partiel étudiant / Student Part-Time Professor Date Posted (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/08/26 Applications must be received BEFORE (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/09/26 Expected Enrolment: 60 Approval date: 2026/08/26 Number of credits: 3 Work Hours: 39 Hourly Rate: Enseignement / Teaching: $239.47 (2024-2025) The academic year starts on September 1 and ends on August 31. These rates do not included vacation pay nor statutory pay. These rates will be applied until a new collective agreement is ratified. Retro will be paid after the ratification. Course type: C Posting type: Régulier / Regular Language of instruction: Anglais | English Competence in second language: Passive Course Schedule: Mardi | Tuesday 8:30-11:30 - - Requirements: Must have an MBA or Master's degree (Preference will be given to a candidate with a PhD – completed or in process of being completed) in an area related to strategic management. Excellent knowledge of course subject matter, demonstrated by having taught similar or related courses, or by recent professional experience directly related to the course. Must preferably also demonstrate experience in using Intopia Strategy Simulation. Teaching mode: Please note that the teaching method will be delivered in person. Teaching method might incur changes due to health measures or other reasons. Additional Information and/or Comments: This section first prioritizes PhD. candidates in an area related to strategic management An acceptable level of education and/or experience could be viewed as being equivalent to the educational required and/or demonstrated experience. If you are invited to continue the selection process, please notify us of any adaptive measures you might require. Information you send us will be handled respectfully and in complete confidence. Employees are required under provincial law to successfully complete all mandatory legislated training. The list of training may be modified by provincial law. The hiring process will be governed by the current APTPUO collective agreements; you can click here for the main unit , here for the OLBI unit , or here for the Toronto/Windsor unit to find out more. The University of Ottawa embraces diversity and inclusion in the workplace. We are passionate about our people and committed to employment equity. We foster a culture of respect, teamwork and inclusion, where collaboration, innovation, and creativity fuel our quest for research and teaching excellence. While all qualified persons are invited to apply, we welcome applications from qualified Indigenous persons, racialized persons, persons with disabilities, women and LGBTQIA2S+ persons. The University is committed to creating and maintaining an accessible, barrier-free work environment. The University is also committed to working with applicants with disabilities requesting accommodation during the recruitment, assessment and selection processes. Applicants with disabilities may contact vra.affairesprofessorales@uottawa.ca to communicate the accommodation need. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Prior to May 1, 2022, the University required all students, faculty, staff, and visitors (including contractors) to be fully vaccinated against Covid-19 as defined in Policy 129 – Covid-19 Vaccination. This policy was suspended effective May 1, 2022 but may be reinstated at any point in the future depending on public health guidelines and the recommendations of experts."
    },
    "https://uottawa.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uOttawa_External_Career_Site/job/Ottawa-ON/Assistant-Professor---in-Artificial-Intelligence-Ethics_JR38647": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - in Artificial Intelligence Ethics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosting Reason: New Position Job Family: Academic Leadership and Faculty Union affiliation: APUO Faculty/Department: Department of Philosophy_Professors and Researchers Campus: Main Campus Date Posted (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/08/26 Applications must be received BEFORE (YYYY/MM/DD): The Department of Philosophy in the Faculty of Arts at the University of Ottawa is seeking applications fоr a tenurе-trасk Assistant Professor position specializing in Artificial Intelligence Ethics, including the philosophical and normative underpinnings of artificial intelligence, along with the philosophical challenges that arise from its applications and repercussions in political, legal, and teсhnоlоgiсаl spheres. The successful candidate will also be responsible for managing and contributing to the development of the interdisciplinary Master's program in Artificial Intelligence Ethics. The area of expertise for this role is flexible. The University of Ottawa is recognized nationally and internationally as a leading university and the largest bilingual university (French and English) in the world. Located on the unceded territory of the Anishinaabe-Algonquin people, in the heart of downtown Ottawa, it contributes significantly to the economy, culture, and quality of life in Canada’s capital. The аntiсipаted start date fоr this pоsitiоn is July 1st, 2027 Position Title: Assistant Professor Duties: The duties of a faculty member include, in varying proportions: a) teaching activities; b) scholarly activities manifested through research and peer-reviewed publications; c) activities related to service to the university community; and d) supervision of graduate students. A commitment to developing discipline and academic unity, including graduate programs, is required. To this end, the successful candidate must have established a rigorous research program that includes grants from major funding agencies such as SSHRC or a clearly defined plan to develop an active research program. The successful candidate will be expected to teach at the undergraduate and graduate levels, in English and French, upon attainment of tenure. Terms: New tenure-track position. Salary: The starting salary for an Assistant Professor is $99,377 (according to the scale in effect as of May 1, 2025). Benefits package: The University of Ottаwа provides an ехtensive benefits package , which includes long-term disability coverage, basic life insurance, supplementary health benefits, a pension plan, optional life insurance, and reimbursement fоr relaxation expenses. Work location: Department of Philosophy, University of Ottawa, 55 Laurier East, 8th Floor, Ottawa, Ontario K1N 6N5 Contact (for inquiries): Dr. Patrice Philie, Director, Department of Philosophy, University of Ottawa, email: Dir.Philosophie-Philosophy.Dir@uottawa.ca . Required qualifications: A Ph.D. in Philosophy or a related discipline completed no later than July 1, 2027; Evidence of an established and innovative research program, together with a record of peer-reviewed publications and scholarly presentations; Demonstrated ability to secure external research funding; Successful teaching experience at the post-secondary level; Have excellent communication skills in French or English. French-English bilingualism is an asset. Active knowledge of Canada’s two official languages (French and English) is a requirement for tenure. Experience recruiting and supervising graduate students (an asset). Deadline: Applications received by October 16, 2026 , will be fully соnsiderеd; however, the position will remain open until it is filled. Further details about academic cаrееrs can be found online. Applications must be submitted through the University of Ottawa’s career portal, and only complete submissions will be evaluated. Plеasе submit the following dосuments in а single PDF: a соver letter, a curriculum vitae, two recent pеer-rеviewed publications, a statement of research interests, and a sample course outline. After an initial screening of applications, shortlisted саndidаtеs will be invited to present their research and conduct a teaching demonstration fоr the Department’s faculty and students. Candidates must also provide three соnfidential letters of recommendation, which should be sent directly by their referees. To learn more about our department, please visit: https://www.uottawa.ca/faculty-arts/philosophy The University of Ottawa is committed to ensuring equity, diversity, and inclusion in the scholarly and leadership environments of our students, staff, and faculty. Accordingly, we strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples in Canada, visible minorities members (racialized persons), persons with disabilities, women, as well as from all qualified candidates with the skills and knowledge to productively engage with equitable, diverse, and inclusive communities. Candidates who wish to be considered as a member of one or more designated groups are asked to complete the confidential Self-Identification Questionnaire, to be completed at the time of application.   All qualified candidates are invited to apply; however, preference will be given to Canadians and permanent residents. When submitting your application, please indicate if you are legally entitled to work in Canada   The University of Ottawa provides accommodations for applicants with disabilities throughout the recruitment process. If you are invited to proceed in the selection process, please notify us of any accommodations that you require by contacting the Office of the Vice-Provost, Faculty Relations by email at vra.affairesprofessorales@uottawa.ca . Any information you send us will be handled respectfully and in complete confidence.   The University of Ottawa is proud of its 160-year tradition of bilingualism. Through its Official Languages and Bilingualism Institute, the University provides training to staff members and to their spouses in their second official language.   Prior to May 1, 2022, the University required all students, faculty, staff, and visitors (including contractors) to be fully vaccinated against Covid-19 as defined in Policy 129 – Covid-19 Vaccination. This policy was suspended effective May 1, 2022 but may be reinstated at any point in the future depending on public health guidelines and the recommendations of experts."
    },
