    "https://uottawa.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uOttawa_External_Career_Site/job/Main-Campus/ATPUO---Winter-2027---ADM3316M---Competitive-intelligence_JR38705": {
      "title": "ATPUO - Winter 2027 - ADM3316M - Competitive intelligence",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosting Reason: New Position Location: Ottawa, ON Academic Period: 2027 Winter Semester Faculty: École de gestion Telfer / Telfer School of Management Academic Unit: Telfer School of Management Course Title: Competitive Intelligence Course Code: ADM3316 Section: M Course Description: Main elements of competitive intelligence and understanding of fundamental issues. Concepts of competitive intelligence, market insight, foresight, peripheral vision and analytics will be used to better understand and use relevant commercial information. Posting limited to: Professeur à temps-partiel régulier / Regular Part-Time Professor Date Posted (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/08/24 Applications must be received BEFORE (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/09/24 Expected Enrolment: 80 Approval date: 2026/08/24 Number of credits: 3 Work Hours: 39 Hourly Rate: Enseignement / Teaching: $239.47 (2024-2025) The academic year starts on September 1 and ends on August 31. These rates do not included vacation pay nor statutory pay. These rates will be applied until a new collective agreement is ratified. Retro will be paid after the ratification. Course type: C Posting type: Régulier / Regular Language of instruction: Anglais | English Competence in second language: Passive Course Schedule: Jeudi | Thursday 8:30-11:30 - - Requirements: Must have a Master's degree with courses or certificates in a business or business related area and have taken courses involving competitive intelligence (eg decision making, non-verbal communications).  Must demonstrate professional experience in intelligence either at the government or industry level. Teaching mode: Please note that the teaching method will be delivered in person. Teaching method might incur changes due to health measures or other reasons. Additional Information and/or Comments: An acceptable level of education and/or experience could be viewed as being equivalent to the educational req