    "https://uottawa.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uOttawa_External_Career_Site/job/Main-Campus/ATPUO---Winter-2027----ADM4348M---Special-Topics-in-Financial-Accounting_JR38616": {
      "title": "ATPUO - Winter 2027 -  ADM4348M - Special Topics in Financial Accounting",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosting Reason: New Position Location: Ottawa, ON Academic Period: 2027 Winter Semester Faculty: École de gestion Telfer / Telfer School of Management Academic Unit: Telfer School of Management Course Title: Special Topics in Financial Accounting Course Code: ADM4348 Section: M Course Description: Covers specialized topics in financial reporting, including accounting for not-for-profit organizations, leases, benefit plans, and corporate income taxes. Posting limited to: Professeur à temps-partiel régulier / Regular Part-Time Professor Date Posted (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/08/24 Applications must be received BEFORE (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/09/24 Expected Enrolment: 60 Approval date: 2026/08/24 Number of credits: 3 Work Hours: 39 Hourly Rate: Enseignement / Teaching: $239.47 (2024-2025) The academic year starts on September 1 and ends on August 31. These rates do not included vacation pay nor statutory pay. These rates will be applied until a new collective agreement is ratified. Retro will be paid after the ratification. Course type: C Posting type: Régulier / Regular Language of instruction: Anglais | English Competence in second language: Passive Course Schedule: Jeudi | Thursday 8:30-11:30 - - Requirements: Should have an MBA or Master's degree (PhD preferred) in the area of financial accounting. Must demonstrate recent professional experience in accounting (including evidence of recently undertaken professional development in the area of IFRS) and have extenvise knowledge of financial reporting; including not-for-profit accounting, leases, pensions and future taxes. Knowledge of both International Financial Reporting Standards (IFRS) and Accounting standards for private enterprises (ASPE) is required. Must also have teaching experience, preferably in this area. Must have a professional accounting designation (CA, CMA or CGA). Teaching mode: Please note that the teaching method will be deliv