    "https://uottawa.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uOttawa_External_Career_Site/job/Ottawa-ON/APTPUO---Aut-Fall-2026---Hiver-Winter-2027-MUS3944-A-1-2---Musique-de-chambre-I-Chamber-Music-I_JR35999": {
      "title": "APTPUO - Aut./Fall 2026 & Hiver/Winter 2027 MUS3944 A 1&2 - Musique de chambre I/Chamber Music I",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-15\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nPosting Reason: New Position Location: Main Campus Academic Period: 2026 Fall - Winter 2027 Faculty: Faculté des arts / Faculty of Arts Academic Unit: École de musique \\\\ School of Music Course Title: Musique de chambre I / Chamber Music I Course Code: MUS39441 & MUS39442 Section: A Course Description: Étude pratique du répertoire de musique de chambre depuis le duo jusqu'aux ensembles plus importants. (Partie 1 de 2) / A practical study of chamber music from duos to larger ensembles. Le nombre de postes et le nombre d'heures pourraient varier selon les inscriptions / The number positions and the number of hours might change according to registration. COURS COMBINÉS: MUS39441 &MUS39442 A - Musique de chambre I/Chamber Music I MUS39451 & MUS39452 A - Musique de chambre II/Chamber Music II MUS49441 & MUS49442 A - Musique de chambre III/Chamber Music III MUS69111 & MUS69112 A - Musique de chambre I/Chamber Music I MUS69131 & MUS69132 A - Musique de chambre II/Chamber Music II MUS69201 & MUS69202 A - Musique de chambre pour diplôme d'études supérieures en interprétation (Partie 1 de 2) / Chamber Music for Graduate Diploma in Performance Cours à l'année / Year long course Mode d'enseignement: en personne Delivery mode: In person Posting limited to: Professeur à temps-partiel régulier / Regular Part-Time Professor Date Posted (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/06/10 Applications must be received BEFORE (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/09/17 Expected Enrolment: n/a Approval date: 2026/09/15 Number of credits: 3 Work Hours: 16 Hourly Rate: Cours d’instruments de musique / Applied Music: $87.76 (2024-2025) The academic year starts on September 1 and ends on August 31. These rates do not included vacation pay nor statutory pay. These rates will be applied until a new collective agreement is ratified. Retro will be paid after the ratification. Course type: D Posting type: Irrégulier / Irregular Language of instruction: Anglais | English, Français | French Competence in second language: Active Course Schedule: - - - L'horaire sera déterminé avec les étudiants / Schedule will be fixed with the students. Requirements: Maîtrise en musique ou l'équivalent; expérience importante comme musicien orchestral; grande connaissance du répertoire de musique de chambre ; vaste expérience comme de coach de musique de chambre; membre d’un orchestre de renom; expertise des cuivres graves (trombone, euphonium et tuba); expérience de l'enseignement au niveau universitaire. / Master's degree in music or equivalent; extensive experience as an orchestral musician; knowledge of chamber music repertoire; wide experience as a chamber music coach; experience in a major orchestra; expertise in low brass instruments (trombone, euphonium and tuba); experience in teaching at university level. Additional Information and/or Comments: Cours à l'année / Year long course 8 semaines par session / 8 weeks per term An acceptable level of education and/or experience could be viewed as being equivalent to the educational required and/or demonstrated experience. If you are invited to continue the selection process, please notify us of any adaptive measures you might require. Information you send us will be handled respectfully and in complete confidence. Employees are required under provincial law to successfully complete all mandatory legislated training. The list of training may be modified by provincial law. The hiring process will be governed by the current APTPUO collective agreements; you can click here for the main unit , here for the OLBI unit , or here for the Toronto/Windsor unit to find out more. The University of Ottawa embraces diversity and inclusion in the workplace. We are passionate about our people and committed to employment equity. We foster a culture of respect, teamwork and inclusion, where collaboration, innovation, and creativity fuel our quest for research and teaching excellence. While all qualifi